; --------------------------------------------------------------------
; Sockets
;
; x86_64 keeps its own legacy syscall table, so every number here
; differs from the aarch64 file beside it - the same reason `read` is 0
; here and 63 there. THE NEAR-MISSES ARE THE HAZARD: `fcntl` is 72 here
; and 25 on aarch64, where 72 is `pselect6`; `socket` is 41 here and 198
; there. A number copied from the wrong file calls something else and
; answers something plausible rather than -ENOSYS.
;
; Verified against the vendored `libc` crate's x86_64 tables and
; cross-checked against `linux-raw-sys`'s kernel-generated constants.
; Not executed here; `scripts/check-cross-targets.sh` proves this file
; compiles and CI on Linux is what runs it.
; --------------------------------------------------------------------
; socket(domain, type, protocol) - 41.
(pub :: sysSocketNum Int)

(pub fn (sysSocketNum) 41)

